foolish_server
foolish_server_prof
foolish_hammer
*.o

# AddressSanitizer/UBSan server build + the adversarial fuzz client
# (fuzz_client.c). Both are local-only dev/test binaries — the source is
# tracked, the compiled artifacts are not. See the foolish_server_asan and
# fuzz_client targets in the Makefile.
foolish_server_asan
fuzz_client
sem_fuzz
sem_fuzz_asan

# QUIC/HTTP3/WebTransport build (foolish_server_quic — quic_wt.c). The binary
# statically links libquiche.a (~tens of MB) and is never tracked. `quiche/`
# is the local quiche FFI build (libquiche.a + quiche.h) the Makefile's
# QUICHE_DIR points at — vendored/built out of tree, not committed. See the
# foolish_server_quic target in the Makefile for how to build it.
foolish_server_quic
wt_client
quiche/
*.a

# Stage 2 (SQLite WAL write-behind persistence — DURABILITY.md): the DB file
# + its WAL/shm sidecars are local run state, never tracked. crash_test.sh
# always points --db at a scratch path under a tmp dir for exactly this
# reason, but guard the default (./foolish.db, from a bare `make run`) too.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Profiling artifacts (server/impls/native/profile.sh, PROFILE_HOTPATH.md):
# raw profiler dumps (callgrind.out*, perf.data, sample.txt), the
# callgrind_annotate TEXT they digest into, and any standalone profiling
# binaries are local-only. What IS tracked under bench_results/<label>/ is
# the small human-readable residue: meta.txt (how the run was taken),
# summary.txt, the *.csv tables, and the helgrind digests. The annotated.txt
# dumps are ~1 MB of machine-specific line attribution that PROFILE_HOTPATH.md
# already quotes the load-bearing lines of; regenerate them with profile.sh
# when a number needs re-checking. See PROFILE_HOTPATH.md "Reading the
# bench_results citations".
bench_results/*/raw/
bench_results/*/raw_cache/
bench_results/*/annotated*.txt
bench_results/eval_t2_oracle
bench_results/eval_t3_prod
bench_results/*.o

# Stage 3 (TLS — TLS.md): never commit a private key or cert, self-signed
# test or otherwise. tls_test.sh always generates its own throwaway cert
# under a scratch tmp dir, never in-tree — this is a guard, not the normal
# case.
*.pem
*.crt
*.key

# Raw Helgrind output (TLS.md's race-check) is a large, run-specific dump —
# same "commit only the digested writeup" discipline persistence/profiling
# artifacts above follow.
helgrind*.log
*.valgrind.log
foolish_server_asm

# throwaway compiler-flag A/B variant binaries (cflags experiment)
fs_*
